# Pits and Banks - BONANZA's second FIELD-cell test course (SPEC.md 128.28), built only by the BZSHAPES=1
# knob beside shapes.bbc (whose head says why there are two).  Not shipped; not on the TOUR; the pathway
# reaches it from SHAPE's exit 1.
#
# The same level plate at 2 units:
#  - at the back, a 1-WIDE `bank` chute 4 px deep (a flat bottom between straight banks), an S;
#  - a SHALLOW 2-wide `round` chute 6 px deep with corners both ways: it carries less than row A's;
#  - in front, two PITS: radius 3, 16 px deep, round a HOLE (roll at its middle and you drop through;
#    come in off-centre with speed and the wall carries you round and throws you out over the far lip),
#    and radius 2, 8 px, with NO hole - a dish to circle in.  A fall through the hole respawns on the
#    plate beside it.
course PITS "Pits and Banks"
width  128
origin 480
ball   rubber

floor rect   4  3 31 28  flat 2
chute 1 bank  depth 4  way  6 6 2 way 13 6 way 13 9 way 20 9
chute 2 round depth 6  way 24 4 2 way 24 8 way 29 8 way 29 13
pit   11 21 2 radius 3 depth 16
pit   23 21 2 radius 2 depth 8 hole 0

start 5 4
goal  tile 30 27  flat 2
clock 28 27
target 60
# the ROUTE (SPEC.md 128.28.10): the autopilot through both chutes, across the dish's middle, and across the
# deep pit left to right on row 22, the line that misses its hole (its rim it cannot ride: no run-up)
way 5 4
way 5 6
way 6 6
way 10 6
way 13 6
way 13 8
way 13 9
way 17 9
way 20 9
way 21 9
way 21 11
way 22 3
way 24 3
way 24 4
way 24 6
way 25 8
way 27 8
way 29 9
way 29 12
way 29 14
way 27 17
way 19 17
way 19 21
way 21 21
way 23 21
way 25 21
way 26 21
way 26 25
way 5 25
way 5 22
way 8 22
way 13 22
way 16 22
way 16 26
way 30 27
